Pod Debugging: 

• kubectl get pods -A | grep -v Running - Find troubled pods 
• kubectl describe pod - Full pod story 
• kubectl logs -f --tail=100 - Live log streaming 
• kubectl logs --previous - Check crashed container logs

Quick Troubleshooting: 

• kubectl get events --sort-by='.lastTimestamp' - Recent cluster events 
• kubectl top pods - Resource usage at a glance 
• kubectl get pods -o wide - Show node placement 
• kubectl exec -it pod -- /bin/sh - Jump inside container

Resource Management: 

• kubectl get all -n namespace - Everything in one view 
• kubectl delete pod --grace-period=0 --force - Force kill stuck pods 
• kubectl scale deployment --replicas=3 - Quick scaling 
• kubectl rollout restart deployment - Restart without downtime

Context Switching:

 • kubectl config get-contexts - List all clusters 
 • kubectl config use-context - Switch clusters 
• kubens - Change namespace (requires kubens tool)

Pro Tips: 

• alias k=kubectl - Save keystrokes 
• kubectl api-resources - See all resource types 
• kubectl explain pod.spec - Built-in documentation
